Now I have all the test code and the extended catalog. Let me produce the full audit.

---

## testsmells.org 19-Smell Academic Audit

**Target:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` — MSTest 4.x, .NET 10, `[TestCategory("Integration")]`

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High | 3 | 3 |
| Medium | 1 | 3 |
| Low | 0 | 0 |
| **Total** | **4** | **6** |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 🔴 HIGH 1 — Sleepy Test *(testsmells.org: Sleepy Test)*

**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)
**Rationale:** `Thread.Sleep(3000)` introduces a 3-second wall-clock wait on every run. Even in integration tests, a hard sleep is a smell because it makes the suite slow and non-deterministic (too short → flaky; too long → wasted time).

```csharp
// ❌ Current
Thread.Sleep(3000);
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

```csharp
// ✅ Fix — poll with a timeout instead of a fixed sleep
var cts = new CancellationTokenSource(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));
while (!_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
{
    await Task.Delay(100, cts.Token);
}
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Risk if unfixed:** 3 s added to every CI run; if the notification is occasionally slower, the test becomes flaky.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH 2 — Conditional Test Logic *(testsmells.org: Conditional Test Logic)*

**Test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 94)
**Rationale:** `if/else` on the type of `loaded` means one assertion branch *never* executes per run. The test silently ignores whichever branch doesn't match.

```csharp
// ❌ Current
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

```csharp
// ✅ Fix — split into two focused tests, each with a deterministic setup
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("vip@example.com", "Vip", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("vip@example.com") as PremiumUser;

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** One branch is never tested, giving false confidence.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH 3 — Assertion-Free Test *(testsmells.org: Unknown Test / Empty Test)*

**Test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)
**Rationale:** Inserts 100 rows but asserts *nothing*. The test passes even if every insert silently fails.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — no assertion at all
for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
{
    _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
}
```

```csharp
// ✅ Fix — verify the inserts actually persisted
for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
{
    _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
}

var users = _repository.ListAll();
Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False green — coverage looks healthy but zero behavior is verified.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM 4 — Assertion Roulette *(testsmells.org: Assertion Roulette)*

**Tests:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (4 assertions, line 28), `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` (2 assertions, line 42), `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` (1 assertion, line 122)

The primary offender is `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` with 4 bare assertions and no messages:

```csharp
// ❌ Current — no failure messages on any assertion
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

```csharp
// ✅ Fix — add a message to each assertion
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Auto-generated Id should be positive");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** When a failure occurs in CI, the developer must read the source to locate which property was wrong.

---

### Smells NOT Found (Clean Patterns)

| Smell | Status | Notes |
|-------|--------|-------|
| Mystery Guest | ✅ Clean | Uses in-memory SQLite — no external files, network, or env vars. Appropriately hermetic for integration tests. |
| Eager Test | ✅ Clean | Tests call 1–2 production methods each (Insert + GetByEmail, etc.). Within norms, especially for integration scope. |
| Magic Number Test | ✅ Clean | Counts (3, 10, 100) directly correspond to items added in the same method — self-documenting. |
| Sensitive Equality | ✅ Clean | No `.ToString()` comparisons. |
| Exception Handling | ✅ Clean | No `try`/`catch` blocks in tests. |
| General Fixture | ✅ Clean | `_connection` and `_repository` are used by every test method. |
| Ignored / Disabled Test | ✅ Clean | No `[Ignore]` or skip attributes. |
| Duplicate Assert | ✅ Clean | No repeated identical assertions. |
| Lazy Test | ✅ Clean | Each test exercises a distinct scenario. |
| Redundant Print / Assertion / Default Test / Constructor Init / Empty Test / Resource Optimism | ✅ Clean | None detected. |

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | **Assertion-Free Test** (`BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors`) | Add a count assertion after the loop | ~1 min |
| 2 | **Conditional Test Logic** (`GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType`) | Split into two deterministic tests | ~5 min |
| 3 | **Sleepy Test** (`NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay`) | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with a polling loop + timeout | ~10 min |
| 4 | **Assertion Roulette** (`InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` + others) | Add message strings to all assertions | ~5 min |

**Bottom line:** The suite is largely well-structured — hermetic in-memory database, clean fixtures, no skipped tests. The three High findings are real risks (a test that verifies nothing, a test with a dead branch, and a hard sleep). Fixing those three plus adding assertion messages will bring this suite to a strong standard.
